recast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Missouri remains a Republican-leaning state in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly nine points toward the GOP. The 2028 race is open, with the incumbent president term-limited, meaning both parties will run national tickets rather than home-state favorites. Josh Hawley has publicly ruled out a 2028 White House run, removing one potential home-state angle, though his decision says little about how the state will vote at the top of the ticket.\n\nNo general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available for this race yet, so expectations rest on Missouri's underlying partisan fundamentals. Those fundamentals point to a Republican win of roughly nine points, with wide uncertainty given how early it is and how little race-specific evidence exists. A strong national Democratic environment or an unusually weak Republican ticket could narrow the gap, but the structural lean favors the GOP.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1545, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2074, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1871, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1883, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2013, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.183, "margin": -9.0}]}